{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["The reason for <b>\"And unto them were born children after the flood\"</b> is to hint that although they were fit for children before the flood — for the way of those generations was to beget at sixty — nevertheless they were not born to them even at a hundred, but only after the flood. For HaShem suppressed their source so that they would not bear and perish in the flood, or so that it would be necessary to save many in the ark. And so He did for this entire family, for Lamech was delayed in the genealogy of Noah more than twofold compared to his ancestors, and Noah very much so. This has already been mentioned in Rashi's commentary (Rashi on Genesis 5:32), from Bereshit Rabbah (Bereshit Rabbah 26:2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:26:44.196157183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}